description:
lib.rs:444-451 binds via:

    let mut v = match v {
        serde_json::Value::Object(m) => m,
        _ => return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(
            SetErrorType::InvalidProperties,
        ))),
    };

Idiomatic Rust 1.65+ is:

    let serde_json::Value::Object(mut v) = v else {
        return Err(BackendSetError::SetError(SetError::new(
            SetErrorType::InvalidProperties,
        )));
    };

Same clippy::manual_let_else lint as the existing JMAP-826m.46 finding, but a different site (test_support::MockBackend::create_object in lib.rs vs. MemoryBackend::update_object in memory.rs:1004) and a different refutable pattern (serde_json::Value variant match vs. Option<T> match). The prior /review-rusty pass located the Option-match site but missed this Value-match sibling.

Engineering impact: low (no behavior change). Engineering basis: maintainability and consistency. The MockBackend::update_object and MockBackend::destroy_object impls a few lines below (lib.rs:479 and lib.rs:504) already use the idiomatic let-else form ('let Some(acct) = guard.get_mut(...) else { ... };'). This site is the only holdout inside test_support, and the file is part of what downstream contributors read when copying the metadata-server scaffolding (this is the same 'reference implementation that propagates inconsistency' rationale .46 makes).

The clippy --tests pedantic run flags this site explicitly:

  warning: this could be rewritten as 'let...else'
    --> crate-jmap-metadata-server/src/lib.rs:444:13

It does NOT fire on the non-test clippy run because test_support is gated on #[cfg(test)], which is presumably why the prior pass missed it: the prior reviewer likely ran clippy --no-deps without --tests.

Fix: replace the four-line match with the three-line let-else as shown above. No companion change needed in mail-server (the canonical does not have a test_support module in src/ — its test harness lives in tests/common/, so there is no analogous site to propagate to).
